	"_doc": "Layouts of places (v0.8.0, LayoutGen, LayoutRules): a square is 5 ft. `cells` — what a character of a chunk means; `kinds` — a place's kind by the tag of its site: its shape (building, tunnels, open), family, rooms with roles and their limit, the size and scatter of an open map; `chunks` — parts of maps: `rows` of `cells`, D — a door socket on the edge, letters of `marks` — named floor squares, a blank — leave the map as it is (landmarks). Rotations and mirrors make new variants of a chunk. The chain of picking a chunk: kind and role, family and role, the room's tags, a generic chunk of the size.",
